KZ3 patch 1141 (SPU pass 120): job I/O capture hooks (every channel op, every DMA element, atomic completions)
and a native-job hook at the WWS policy module's job-call bracket. Engine-generic: all hooks null unless a title
installs them (KZ3: port/spu/kz3_jobhook.c). Host tests: tools/spu/test_r120_jobreplay.sh.
Pass 121: selectWorkload answers (kind 6 through the channel hook) and interrupt take/iret (g_spu_jcap_irq,
spu_drain.c + spu_interp.c) reach the capture too, so a replay can serve the kernel's answers and the handler's LS
changes. The job-call bracket closes regardless of host depth for the frame trace and jobcost too (kinds 36/37
in the frame trace mark the closes the depth test lost and brackets that never closed).

